# tally

`tally` prints line, word, and byte counts, like a minimal `wc`.

```sh
go build -o tally .
./tally notes.txt todo.txt
printf 'one two\n' | ./tally -w
```

Flags `-l`, `-w`, and `-c` select lines, words, and bytes; with none, all three
are printed. Each input gets one line of right-aligned columns followed by its
name, and a `total` line follows when more than one file is given.
